[[:db/retract 17592186157806 :question/answer-fields 17592186155727] [:db/retract 17592186157807 :question/answer-fields 17592186155733] {:db/id 17592186157806 :question/problem "Which of the following are logically equivalent to $X?$\n\n- $X∨(X∨Y)$\n- $(Y∧X)∨X$\n- $Y∨(X∧Y)$" :question/worked-solution "The law that disjunction absorbs conjunction is stated as\n\n$$\nX∨(X∧Y)≡X.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is *not* logically equivalent to $X.$ This statement cannot be simplified using the absorption laws.\n\n- Statement II is logically equivalent to $X.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(Y∧X)∨X & ≡X∨(Y∧X) \\\\  & ≡X∨(X∧Y) \\\\  & ≡X.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is *not* logically equivalent to $A.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y∨(X∧Y) & ≡Y∨(Y∧X) \\\\  & ≡Y≢X.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f770988e-367c-568b-b9ad-aed362d52e80"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f770988e-367c-568b-b9ad-aed362d52e80" :answer-field/id #uuid "f770988e-367c-568b-b9ad-aed362d52e80" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0cc9dfdc-588c-582f-9f2b-c80f69517904" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c5ea4095-baee-5787-855f-5de1e85f86e1" "answer-bdb55b9e-b815-5740-9c0c-62a65fdabd92" "answer-1ab4fef3-6b76-545c-a2e2-0dad117ccb95" "answer-e9eb4a13-2ded-5150-8eb6-f810b7f1c872" "answer-0cc9dfdc-588c-582f-9f2b-c80f69517904"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c5ea4095-baee-5787-855f-5de1e85f86e1" :answer/id #uuid "c5ea4095-baee-5787-855f-5de1e85f86e1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bdb55b9e-b815-5740-9c0c-62a65fdabd92" :answer/id #uuid "bdb55b9e-b815-5740-9c0c-62a65fdabd92" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :d